body:
`fetch_json(transport, url, retries=0)` in `apiclient/fetch.py` calls `transport(url)`, which returns `(status, body_text)`. Today it accepts only status 200, raises a bare `ApiError` for everything else, and lets `json.JSONDecodeError` escape. The module already defines the exception classes; please use them:

- any 2xx status: return the parsed JSON body;
- 404: raise `NotFound`;
- any other 4xx: raise `ClientError` with its `status` attribute set to the status code;
- 5xx: call the transport again, up to `retries` more times; if the last attempt is still 5xx, raise `ServerError` with `status` set to the last status code. 4xx responses are never retried;
- a 2xx body that is not valid JSON: raise `BadResponse`, chained from the original `json.JSONDecodeError` (`raise ... from err`);
- any other status: raise `ApiError`.

All of these are subclasses of `ApiError`, so existing `except ApiError` handlers keep working.
